          {
            "title": "_findAndModify missing population support for findOneAndUpdate/findOneAndRemove",
            "severity": "high",
            "file": "lib/query.js",
            "line": 2424,
            "explanation": "The original code in Query.prototype._findAndModify did not handle the case where a query has population options specified. As a result, if the options include 'populate', the returned document from findAndModify will not populate referenced documents, breaking expected behavior.",
            "suggestion": "Check if self.options.populate is set. If not, behave as before. If true, call model.populate on the returned document with the prepared population options before completing the promise. Follow the same pattern as used in findOne and execFind methods for population.",
            "failureAfterChange": "A query with findOneAndUpdate or findOneAndRemove called with population options will now have populated paths in the result, whereas before those paths remained unpopulated (raw ObjectIds).",
